<title>USA: American disappointed by 'open skies' delay.</title>
<headline>American disappointed by 'open skies' delay.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMR Corp's American Airlines said Tuesday it was disappointed at the postponement of &quot;open skies&quot; aviation talks between the United States and Britain but remained hopeful that the delay was only temporary.</p>
<p>The U.S. Department of Transportation said earlier that its officials called off aviation talks scheduled for this week, saying the two sides remained too far apart for productive negotiations.</p>
</text>
